post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

omacrt is installed. Two steps are left, and both are yours to take:

  1. hand the DAC's connector to omacrt at every boot:
       sudo systemctl enable --now omacrt-lease.service
     The connector defaults to HDMI-A-1. For another one:
       sudo systemctl edit omacrt-lease.service
     and set Environment=OMACRT_CONNECTOR=HDMI-A-2

  2. install the bar plugin into your own session (not as root):
       /usr/share/omacrt/omacrt-install --no-build

Then check the setup with:  omacrt doctor

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'

omacrt upgraded. If the bar plugin looks stale, refresh it with:
  /usr/share/omacrt/omacrt-install --no-build

MSG
}

pre_remove() {
  systemctl disable --now omacrt-lease.service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
}
